Surface B — partition module (manifest loader + classifier):

  - NEW file: framework/tools/pos-publish-framework-only/src/loam/
    publish_framework_only/partition.py (~150-250 LOC).
  - Public surface: PartitionClass StrEnum (PUBLIC_ONLY,
    DEV_AND_PUBLIC, DEV_ONLY, EXCLUDED_FROM_PUBLISH);
    PartitionManifest dataclass; ManifestEntry dataclass;
    ManifestError exception; load_manifest(path) -> PartitionManifest;
    classify_path(manifest, ws_rel_path) -> PartitionClass | None;
    is_publishable(klass) -> bool.
  - Schema validation: missing required key, unknown top-level
    key, non-list value, malformed entry, schema_version != 1
    all raise ManifestError.
  - Classification semantics: first-match-wins precedence
    (excluded_from_publish > dev_only > public_only >
    dev_and_public per plan §10 D-build.M2.3). Glob semantics
    mirror loam_mode.manifest._glob_match.
  - __init__.py extended to export the new public surface.

Surface C — synth.py extension:

  - synthesise_framework_only gains required manifest_path: Path
    parameter (per plan §10 D-build.M2.4 — required forces
    callers to decide).
  - Loads manifest via partition.load_manifest; raises
    SynthesisError on schema problems.
  - Walks source commit's tree via `git ls-tree -r <source-sha>`
    to enumerate every leaf path.
  - For each leaf path: audit-exclude check first; then
    partition.classify_path; SynthesisError("partition incomplete:
    <N> unclassified paths: <first-3>...") if any non-audit-
    excluded leaf returns None.
  - Builds synthetic tree from public_only ∪ dev_and_public
    leaves; existing promotion logic (framework/<entry> ->
    root) preserved; existing collision detection preserved.
  - mktree + commit-tree + update-ref unchanged.
  - HARD CUTOVER: FRAMEWORK_PREFIX + TOP_LEVEL_DOCS module-
    level constants RETIRE (deletion per plan §10 D-build.M2.5).

